All right, I've got mucho questions that have been piling up.  I first 
started playing PC Nethack about two weeks ago, and got hooked immediately.
Since then, I've been stockpiling my questions so I could address them to 
the net at large in a lump sum.  Here we go, in no particular order:

1) Wands of wishes.  I've tried wishing for scrolls of charging, but the
wand just blows up on me when I use them.  Is there a trick to this?  Or
are there just a limited number of wishes you can get out of a wand?

2)  Statues.  I understand that some statues will have scrolls in them.  Is
it possible to do anything else with these statues like, say, bring them to 
life?  I know some statues do that when you step on them.  I am also
presuming that there is a difference between a statue and a figurine.  Is
this indeed the case?

3).  Dilithium Crystals.  What on EARTH do these things DO?  I've tried 
everything I can think of, and have no earthly idea what to do with them.
My first thought was that they would act as power sources for magic items
(kinda like the Star Trek crystals do), but I have yet to see how this
would work.

4).  Naming things.  Does naming an elven dagger Sting _actually_ mean 
that the dagger becomes Sting?  And does the same hold true for Orcrist?
I've tried this, but since I really don't need either one (I'm currently
using a +7 Excalibur--yeah, I got _really_ lucky with those scrolls of
enchant weapon :) ), I haven't noticed if they work as expected.  This
is pure laxidaisical attitude on my part, but I also haven't bumped into
a measly orc for awhile, so it's not important.

5).  Level teleport.  Okay, the description of the Amulet of Yendor says
that you can't level teleport while it's in your possession.  Note that
this is while you have it, not while you're wearing it.  I haven't gotten
to the bloody thing yet,  but at least one level in my current dungeon
doesn't have a stair down (one of the levels of Hell; I believe someone
else here evinced a similar problem), so I'm a little concerned about the
trek back up.  Especially if that Yendor geek is gonna be following me!:)

6).  Cursed objects.  When you get the message "You hear a mumbled curse"
do you have any way of knowing what (if anything) you own has been cursed?
I believe the help files mention that once you identify something you always
remain aware of its blessed/cursed status, but does anyone know if there's
a way of telling with items you haven't identified yet?  (Yah, I know the
routine:  Drop it and see if your pet walks over it/picks it up, or drop it
on an altar; I'm looking to see if there's another way without going back
up diddley-ump flights of stairs, since my kitty-cat hacked the big furball
back on level 10 and my replacement winter wolf had the bad judgement to
go toe-to-breath weapon with a dragon; the nearest altar is a bit far away
at the moment to make the trip worth my while.)

and last, but not least:

7).  Holy/Unholy water.  How do you make this stuff?  It's great for lots
of things, but how can you get it?  I've found one, count 'em one, potion
that turned out to be holy water, and one that turned out to be unholy.  If
I weren't doing so well with my current character, I'd start over again as
a priest, just to get the holy water. :)  I had originally thought that 
someone here mentioned you could make it by dropping it on an altar, but that
doesn't seem to work.  Maybe it has to be a lawful altar?  (Wouldn't help me
any, since I've converted all the altars to my neutral god, but it'd be nice
to know in the future...)

Anyway, sorry to take up so much bandwidth, and these questions have probably
been hashed out before, so if you'd rather email than post, that's fine.  I
read this group at least once a day, so I'm bound to see any responses either
way.  Thanks in advance for any help.

The Walrus



